# =============================================================================
# Diligently — Tauri backend environment
# =============================================================================
#
# HOW TO USE
# -----------
# 1. Copy this file to `.env` in this same folder:
#      diligent/src-tauri/.env
# 2. Fill in values below (no quotes needed for simple keys).
# 3. Restart the app (`npm run tauri dev` or the installed binary).
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Commit only `.env.example`.
#
# =============================================================================
# Deepgram — system-audio speech-to-text (Rust `transcribe_audio`)
# =============================================================================
#
# GET AN API KEY
# ---------------
# 1. Open https://console.deepgram.com/
# 2. Sign up or log in.
# 3. Go to **API Keys** → **Create a new API key** (copy it once; you may not see it again).
#
# Docs: https://developers.deepgram.com/docs/authenticating
#
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# Prerecorded / file transcription model (examples: nova-3, nova-2, whisper-large)
DEEPGRAM_MODEL=nova-3

# =============================================================================
# OpenAI & DeepSeek — LLM chat (main window, read automatically from this file)
# =============================================================================
# 
# If `API_KEY`/`MODEL` are empty in Settings for OpenAI or DeepSeek, the app
# now auto-falls back to these env values.
#
# GET OPENAI API KEY
# ------------------
# 1. https://platform.openai.com/
# 2. **API keys** → **Create new secret key** → copy and store safely.
#
# GET DEEPSEEK API KEY
# --------------------
# 1. https://platform.deepseek.com/
# 2. **API keys** (or account/API section) → create key → copy.
#
# Suggested defaults: OpenAI `gpt-4o-mini` (fast/cheap), DeepSeek `deepseek-v4-pro`
# (thinking-mode, best at problem-solving on copied content). Legacy DeepSeek
# IDs `deepseek-chat` / `deepseek-reasoner` deprecate 2026-07-24 — use v4.
#
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v4-pro

# =============================================================================
# Anthropic (Claude) — primary LLM for interview mode (Sonnet 4.6 default)
# =============================================================================
#
# GET AN API KEY
# --------------
# 1. https://console.anthropic.com/ (separate from your claude.ai Pro/Max sub)
# 2. Add billing, prepay credits ($5 minimum, $20 = ~150 interviews)
# 3. Settings → API Keys → Create Key, copy the sk-ant-api03-... immediately
#
# Model IDs:
#   claude-sonnet-4-6 (default — interview audio + screenshot code)
#   claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (speed-priority fallback)
#   claude-opus-4-7 (max-quality escalation — slow + expensive)
#
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# =============================================================================
# Tavily Search — company research (Phase 3 "Research" tab, Rust `web_search`)
# =============================================================================
#
# GET AN API KEY
# --------------
# 1. https://app.tavily.com/  (sign up — free tier, no card required)
# 2. Copy the API key from the dashboard (starts with `tvly-`).
#
# Free tier ~1,000 credits/month; each research run uses ~2 queries
# (search_depth=basic = 1 credit each). Read at runtime from this file (no
# rebuild needed) — restart the app after setting it.
#
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# Optional — hosted “managed” backend (Settings → enable only if you use it)
# =============================================================================
#
# If Managed API is on, these must be set (here and restart, or at compile time via build.rs).
# Default app behavior uses your own provider keys from Settings / OPENAI_* / DEEPSEEK_* above.
#
# APP_ENDPOINT=https://your-managed-api.example
# API_ACCESS_KEY=
# PAYMENT_ENDPOINT=
